    "response": "The consumer is `InvoiceProcessor` in `src/billing/invoice.processor.ts`, registered for the BullMQ `invoices` queue via `@Processor(\"invoices\")`. Its `process` method passes `customerId` and `totalCents` to `InvoiceService.createInvoice`.\n\nCall path:\n\n`InvoiceProcessor.process` → `InvoiceService.createInvoice` → `Repository<Invoice>.save(invoice)`\n\n`createInvoice` first loads the customer, constructs an `Invoice` with `Repository.create`, then performs the actual TypeORM write with `this.invoices.save(invoice)`. The `Invoice` entity maps to the `invoices` table.",
